<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="001" project="spaarkeai-compose-r7">
  <metadata>
    <title>Coordination gate + publish-size baseline + env verification</title>
    <phase>0 Coordination Gate + Baseline</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>MINIMAL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>No source code modified — runs /conflict-check, records a publish-size baseline, and verifies the PDF DI env gate; produces a coordination note only.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical verification + note authoring; no architectural judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Gate task — must complete before any implementation task starts; establishes the shared baseline the whole project cites.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>devops, ci-cd, bff-api, deploy, dotnet-10</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Open the R7 coordination gate: run /conflict-check against the hot-path files, record the current BFF compressed
    publish-size baseline, and confirm the PDF Document-Intelligence compound DI gate state in the target env. Write
    the findings to a coordination note. Do NOT modify any source code in this task.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Familiar with the BFF publish pipeline, /conflict-check, and Azure Document Intelligence configuration. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    A coordination note exists at projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/notes/coordination-baseline.md recording: (0) net10-readiness
    confirmation — branch merged net10 master, `dotnet --list-sdks` shows 10.0.1xx, `dotnet build -c Release` of the BFF is
    clean on net10; (1) /conflict-check result for the R7 hot-path files, (2) measured compressed BFF publish size (absolute) —
    the **net10** baseline (the ~46.94 MB figure cited in spec/plan was the net8 R6 baseline; this task re-measures on net10 and
    that number supersedes it for all downstream NFR-01 delta reporting), (3) confirmed on/off state of the PDF intake compound
    DI gate in the target env, (4) status of watched PRs (#690 ci-lfs, #266 OpenXml).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Phase 0 of plan.md. R7 touches shared spine files that overlap active sibling worktrees (spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r3
      on ConversationPane.tsx/SprkChatInput.tsx; spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2 sole-owner of Services/Ai/). Every BFF-touching
      task must report publish size vs the ~46.94 MB R6 baseline (NFR-01), so we capture the true current baseline once, here.
      FR-06 requires the compound gate Analysis:Enabled &amp;&amp; DocumentIntelligence:Enabled to be ON in the target env.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="doc-output">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/notes/coordination-baseline.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/AnalysisServicesModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/INDEX.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">This task MUST NOT modify any .cs/.ts/.tsx source; it is read-only + note authoring.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Publish-size measurement MUST use the repo-standard command: dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/, then measure compressed output; state the PDB convention (incl. or excl. PDBs) when reporting, per root §10.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The env DI gate is at AnalysisServicesModule.cs:154 (compound Analysis:Enabled &amp;&amp; DocumentIntelligence:Enabled). Record whether the target env has both ON; if OFF, note that PDF intake will degrade to NullComposePdfIntakeSource typed "PDF intake unavailable" (FR-06 acceptance would then fail in that env).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>coordination, publish-size, env verification</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/graph6-kiota2-break-assessment.md</file>
      <file>projects/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor MINIMAL; load spec.md + CLAUDE.md + bff-extensions.md.</step>
    <step order="0.5" name="net10-readiness">Confirm the branch is on net10 master (git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/master == 0), `dotnet --list-sdks` shows a 10.0.1xx entry, and `dotnet build -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` is clean. If build flags Graph/Kiota call sites, consult projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/graph6-kiota2-break-assessment.md. Record net10-ready = yes/no. (Baseline done at init 2026-08-14: branch merged net10 master, Release build clean.)</step>
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check focused on ConversationPane.tsx, SprkChatInput.tsx, Services/Ai/**, Services/Compose/**. Record the result.</step>
    <step order="2">Run dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/ (on net10); measure the compressed size; record absolute MB + the PDB convention. This is the **net10** baseline that supersedes the net8 ~46.94 MB figure for all downstream NFR-01 delta reporting.</step>
    <step order="3">Inspect AnalysisServicesModule.cs:154 and the target-env config to confirm the compound PDF DI gate state; record ON/OFF.</step>
    <step order="4">Check the status of watched PRs #690 (ci-lfs) and #266 (OpenXml bump); note any relevance to FR-13 / dependency bumps.</step>
    <step order="5">Write projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/notes/coordination-baseline.md with all four findings.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 001 status to ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If /conflict-check reports an active conflicting PR on ConversationPane.tsx / SprkChatInput.tsx / Services/Ai files, STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md §6) with the conflicting PR before any Phase 1/6/7 task that touches those files proceeds.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/publish the BFF for size measurement</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run /conflict-check, gh PR status</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/notes/coordination-baseline.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The note records net10-readiness: branch 0 behind net10 master, SDK 10.0.1xx visible, BFF Release build clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The coordination note records a /conflict-check result for the four hot-path file groups.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note records the measured compressed BFF publish size in MB and states the PDB convention.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note records the on/off state of the compound PDF DI gate in the target env, with the NullObject-degradation consequence if OFF.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note records the status of PRs #690 and #266.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No source file (.cs/.ts/.tsx) was modified by this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md Phase 0 / plan.md §Phase 0. This baseline is cited by every downstream BFF task (010/013/050/073/074) for NFR-01 delta reporting.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
